	If anyone has read the Pliocene Exile saga plus _Jack the Bodiless_ by
Julian May, what do you think of CE interface armor? Pretend for the moment
that telepathy in Nethack is a low level equivalent to metapsychic suboperancy.
CE helmet, CE suit (the generator might cause problems -- "there is a CE rig
here, but you cannot carry anymore" :-)  I think maybe just the helmet. I know
that telekinesis has been bandied about as a use of "Pw" which has hardly been
pushed to its full potential.  PK + EE (AC -30 astral projection, if you get
"killed" you pop back into your body minus all current Pw) + ultrasenses (a
Meta-key ;-) that lets you perform the function of a stethoscope) + creativity
(enhance AC temporarily with high drain on Pw) + coercion/redaction (since
there are no "psionic" attacks in NH as it is except possibly paralysis by
floating eye, stun/confusion by demon lords, and seduction, these functions
would be hard to implement). You might make only a certain small percentage
fully operant (via intrinsic), something that can't be gained as the intrinsic
if you don't enter the game with it, but if a torc is found...
Real operants are automatically telepathic, but the minimal level of latency
required to be raised by a torc (Amulet of Metapsychic Operancy) requires
telepathy. Without it, the hapless hacker undergoes black torc syndrome
(Sickness) and will need divine assistance just to remove the amulet. CE armor
is only useful as regular armor (doing a bit of damage when you put it on), but
worn by an operant (even a torced one), it doubles Pw and greatly increases
the effects of metafunctions. Oh, and of course farsensing operants don't need
a blindfold to get the monster-detection effect.


